@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+---
+id: task-004-hourly-rental-for-periods-under-a-day
+type: task
+title: "Hourly rental for periods under a day"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Hourly rental for periods under a day
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and the desk turns them away today. Customers can rent by
+the hour. `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice`: the price of one hour of rental in integer euro
+cents.
+
+## Scope
+
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice, hourlyPrice? })`: `hourlyPrice`, when given, is a non-negative integer
+  number of cents. When it is omitted, the item has no hourly price. Anything else for `hourlyPrice` is rejected.
+- A rental shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour is an hourly rental. Its total is the number of
+  hours times `hourlyPrice`. "On the hour" means minutes, seconds and milliseconds are all zero, in UTC.
+- An item without an hourly price cannot be rented by the hour: `quote` and `book` reject such a period.
+- An hourly rental is not discounted by the long-stay rule of task-003 (it is always shorter than a day).
+- `quote`, `book` and `availability` accept hourly periods. `book` returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`
+  as before. `start` and `end` in the results are ISO-8601 UTC strings with the milliseconds shown, as today.
+- Overlap rules are unchanged: an hourly booking blocks overlapping periods of the same item, and a period that
+  only touches the end or start of a booking does not overlap it.
+- Whole-day rentals keep their rules: a period of one day or more still starts and ends at UTC midnight.
+
+## Rules
+
+Task-001 applies, with one change to its rule 3 for periods shorter than a day:
+
+- A period of one day or more must still start and end at UTC midnight, as before.
+- A period shorter than a day must start and end on the hour (UTC). It is priced hourly, so the item needs a
+  `hourlyPrice`.
+- A period of exactly 24 hours that does not start at midnight is not a whole day and is not shorter than a
+  day, so it is still rejected.
+- The end must still be after the start.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1: `addEquipment` accepts an item with an `hourlyPrice`, and an item without one.
+- AC2: `addEquipment` rejects an `hourlyPrice` that is not a non-negative integer number of cents.
+- AC3: an hourly period of 3 hours on an item with `hourlyPrice` 800 has total 2400.
+- AC4: `quote` and `book` for the same hourly period return the same total.
+- AC5: a period shorter than a day that starts or ends off the hour (for example 10:30) is rejected.
+- AC6: a period shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour, and crosses midnight, is priced by the
+  hours it covers (for example 23:00 to 01:00 is 2 hours).
+- AC7: an item without an hourly price rejects an hourly period in `quote` and `book`.
+- AC8: a period of one day or more that does not start and end at UTC midnight is still rejected, including a
+  24-hour period starting at 10:00.
+- AC9: an hourly booking blocks an overlapping hourly or whole-day period of the same item; a period that
+  touches it at its start or end is accepted.
+- AC10: `availability` includes hourly periods: an item booked for an overlapping hour is not listed, and an
+  item booked for a touching period is listed.
+- AC11: the long-stay discount does not apply to hourly rentals, and whole-day rentals are priced as before.
+- AC12: a period that ends before or at its start is still rejected.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Changes rule 3 of task-001 for periods shorter than a day (AC2 and AC5 of task-001 are narrowed to whole-day
+and off-the-hour periods) and extends task-002 to hourly periods. The tests that asserted that a period shorter
+than a day starting at 10:00 is rejected are replaced by tests of AC5 and AC8. Each acceptance criterion maps
+to one or more tests in `src/rental.test.ts`.
